# motoquencer: the randomize-CV detents scale the offset linearly (issue #57).
# motoquencer.md: "The other 7 steps will increasingly modify the step's CV" —
# detent 7 is the full +/- cvrange/2, so detent n is n/7 of that.
#
# Same trick as randomize-spread.gold: continuous pitch, cvrange 1, the step
# dialed to 0.5, so the output is 0.5 + u * (n/7) * 0.5 for the seed-1 uniform
# draws u in [-1, +1). Detent 1 keeps the note within +/- 1/14 of the dialed
# value; detent 3 spreads three times as far — the same three draws that moved
# the note by 0.071 at detent 1 would move it by 0.214 here.
seed 1
tickrate 100
patch <<<
[m4]
[motoquencer]
    numfaders = 1
    numsteps  = 1
    clock     = I1
    fadermode = I2
    quantize  = 0
    cvbase    = 0
    cvrange   = 1
    holdcv    = 0
    cv        = O1
>>>
# randomize lane: detent 1 of 0..7 (slight randomization)
@1 set I2 1
@2 move F1 0.1428571
@3 expect F1 0.1428571 tol 1e-4
@4 set I2 0
@5 move F1 0.5
# 0.5 + u/14
@10 set I1 1
@10 expect O1 0.4285804 tol 1e-5
@11 set I1 0
@12 set I1 1
@12 expect O1 0.4308211 tol 1e-5
@13 set I1 0
@14 set I1 1
@14 expect O1 0.5166291 tol 1e-5
@15 set I1 0
# same fader, detent 3 (strong randomization) — the CV lane keeps its 0.5
@16 set I2 1
@17 move F1 0.4285714
@18 expect F1 0.4285714 tol 1e-4
@19 set I2 0
# 0.5 + 3u/14
@22 set I1 1
@22 expect O1 0.3164080 tol 1e-5
@23 set I1 0
@24 set I1 1
@24 expect O1 0.5250664 tol 1e-5
@25 set I1 0
@26 set I1 1
@26 expect O1 0.3601032 tol 1e-5
